v 3
d freeiv: Instrument-free estimation of a linear structural model
d
d  freeiv estimates the coefficient on an endogenous regressor without an
d  external instrument.  Under scale consistency alone -- the confounder's
d  direct loading in the outcome equation is proportional to its loading in
d  the first stage -- the coefficient is bounded by [gamma-tilde/2,
d  gamma-tilde], where gamma-tilde is the OLS slope, and that interval is
d  exactly the region where the implied variances are non-negative.  Every
d  point estimator adds one assumption to close the system; the package shows
d  them side by side against the interval so that each can be judged.
d
d  Routes implemented: the identified set; the quadratic moment estimator
d  (default), which needs only a non-zero third moment of the confounder; the
d  cubic under equal variances and its scale-free counterpart; the
d  higher-moment estimator; quantile bias extrapolation; two GMM routes on the
d  moments of orders two, three and four, each with its over-identification
d  test -- the joint nine-moment estimator of Araar (2026c), minimised on a
d  deterministic two-dimensional grid rather than by multi-start, which also
d  returns the region of gamma where the profiled Hansen statistic is within
d  3.84 of its minimum, and the profiled variant, which is one-dimensional and
d  needs no optimiser at all; Lewbel, Schennach and Zhang (2024) as trigmm
d  implements it; and, for comparison on the same data, Lewbel (2012), the
d  Gaussian copula, the rank control function, and Oster (2019).
d
d  Two endogenous variables sharing one latent confounder switch to the
d  two-indicator model, where the confounder's direct loading is free and
d  identified -- which is what makes scale consistency itself testable.
d
d  Companion commands: freeivmenu says which routes the data can carry before
d  any estimation; freeivdiag says what a value of gamma implies about the
d  unobservables, whatever produced it; freeivtest reports endogeneity,
d  agreement between routes, and an outside estimate against the identified
d  set; freeivreport assembles all of it into one table.
d
d  Four datasets travel with the package and are retrieved with -net get
d  freeiv-.  Three are simulated and their generating equations are printed in
d  help freeiv, so none is a black box: freeiv_sim1 satisfies the model and the
d  true coefficient is known, freeiv_sim2 differs from it only in that the
d  first-stage disturbance is skewed, which invalidates the symmetry route and
d  leaves the others intact, and freeiv_proxy carries two endogenous regressors
d  loading on one confounder.  The fourth, freeiv_card, is the Card (1995)
d  extract used in the empirical section of Araar (2026d), distributed with
d  Wooldridge's teaching datasets; on it a single endogenous regressor can only
d  be bounded, while a second indicator of the same confounder identifies it,
d  which is the argument of that paper on its own data.
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260915
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar, Universite Laval and PEP
d Support: email aabd@ecn.ulaval.ca
d
